WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:07.045
On February 24,

00:00:07.045 --> 00:00:09.548
my daughter spoke for the first time.

00:00:10.257 --> 00:00:13.593
First word was “ba-bah,”

00:00:13.635 --> 00:00:16.429
which means the sound
of a great explosion.

00:00:17.055 --> 00:00:21.017
That night, we woke
to the concussive sound of bombs

00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:23.270
as our windows came crashing in.

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:26.022
It was the bombardment of Kyiv.

00:00:26.523 --> 00:00:29.609
I'm someone who didn't believe
it would happen.

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:34.114
I was born just a few days
before the Chernobyl disaster

00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:36.992
and a few years before the collapse
of the Soviet Union.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:40.370
I grew up in an independent Ukraine,

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:43.707
struggling to overcome the legacy
of the Soviet system.

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:47.919
My mother and my grandmother
worked very hard

00:00:47.961 --> 00:00:50.964
so that I could have a good education

00:00:51.006 --> 00:00:54.759
because they believed
my generation would build the country.

00:00:55.427 --> 00:00:56.678
And we have.

00:00:57.178 --> 00:00:59.514
Until six weeks ago,

00:00:59.556 --> 00:01:02.267
Ukraine was on an upward path,

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:05.895
becoming more prosperous,
more fair, more free.

00:01:06.855 --> 00:01:10.525
In 2004 and 2013,

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:14.821
we marched for democracy,
and we defeated autocracy.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.451
So I was stunned
when the windows crushed in.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:21.786
I froze.

00:01:22.412 --> 00:01:25.540
Speechless, motionless,

00:01:25.582 --> 00:01:27.792
absolutely helpless.

00:01:28.627 --> 00:01:31.004
That was my first lesson of war.

00:01:32.047 --> 00:01:35.925
What you cherish can be taken
from you in a moment.

00:01:36.718 --> 00:01:38.887
Even your peace of mind.

00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:45.644
My hands were still shaking as I fled
to the west of Ukraine with my children

00:01:45.644 --> 00:01:47.771
and then over the border to Slovakia.

00:01:48.104 --> 00:01:53.193
My husband and my parents remain
in Kyiv, helping our country.

00:01:54.235 --> 00:01:56.696
As we traveled further from our family,

00:01:56.738 --> 00:01:59.824
I imagined all that was being destroyed.

00:01:59.866 --> 00:02:03.244
Our homes, our hospitals,

00:02:03.286 --> 00:02:07.540
our critical infrastructure
and so much more.

00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:10.919
For 40 million people in my country

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:13.713
and for billions around the globe,

00:02:13.713 --> 00:02:18.301
February 24 is the day
Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.638
For seven million Ukrainian children,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.600
it is also the day
Russia tried to take their future.

00:02:26.643 --> 00:02:32.065
176 children have been killed
by Russian bombs.

00:02:32.482 --> 00:02:34.776
Hundreds more have been wounded.

00:02:35.902 --> 00:02:37.070
Ten years ago,

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:40.448
I dedicated myself
to building world-class schools

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:42.117
for the children of Ukraine.

00:02:43.118 --> 00:02:46.246
I believe education
is the most powerful tool

00:02:46.246 --> 00:02:48.498
for improving the economy,

00:02:48.498 --> 00:02:51.334
the environment and human well-being.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:55.296
War very quickly destroys all three.

00:02:55.964 --> 00:03:00.301
So far, 900 schools
have been critically damaged.

00:03:00.343 --> 00:03:02.887
84 are completely destroyed.

00:03:03.513 --> 00:03:06.099
And yet, education goes on.

00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:08.560
During the COVID pandemic,

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:14.524
Ukrainian government engaged my team
to create the Ukrainian school online.

00:03:15.024 --> 00:03:16.526
During the last two years,

00:03:16.526 --> 00:03:20.321
it has delivered school to children
wherever they were.

00:03:21.072 --> 00:03:25.368
Students from remote areas
had access to teachers and lessons

00:03:25.368 --> 00:03:27.704
they wouldn't have otherwise.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.499
This platform covers the secondary
school curriculum

00:03:31.541 --> 00:03:36.212
and puts every student in front
of our very best teachers.

00:03:37.464 --> 00:03:42.594
We never imagined our nonprofit
project would be needed in a situation

00:03:42.635 --> 00:03:45.805
even more horrible than COVID.

00:03:47.056 --> 00:03:52.562
But today, almost 400,000 students
learn on this platform.

00:03:52.604 --> 00:03:57.734
They connect from within Ukraine
and from 120 countries

00:03:57.776 --> 00:03:59.903
where they are refugees at the moment.

00:04:01.446 --> 00:04:05.200
And for all of them,
those couple of hours a day

00:04:05.241 --> 00:04:08.703
is not just a safe environment
where they learn something new.

00:04:09.204 --> 00:04:13.500
It is also the space where,
despite everything,

00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:16.961
Ukraine continues to invest in them.

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:20.799
And that was my second lesson of war.

00:04:21.382 --> 00:04:24.427
Putin can take a lot from us.

00:04:24.928 --> 00:04:29.933
Our homes, our jobs,
our loved ones, our peace.

00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:33.645
But he cannot undo education.

00:04:34.103 --> 00:04:38.191
Knowledge and curiosity
are unassailable treasures.

00:04:38.775 --> 00:04:41.986
And as long as our children keep learning

00:04:42.028 --> 00:04:44.781
and our teachers keep teaching,

00:04:44.823 --> 00:04:48.701
even while they are starving
in shelters under bombardment,

00:04:48.743 --> 00:04:50.912
even in refugee camps,

00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:53.164
we are undefeated.

00:04:54.874 --> 00:04:59.087
In this war, every Ukrainian
has his own front.

00:04:59.128 --> 00:05:03.591
Our soldiers, our doctors, our mothers.

00:05:04.092 --> 00:05:07.220
And, yes, even our children and teachers.

00:05:07.637 --> 00:05:12.100
By continuing to learn,
they fight for our future.

00:05:13.393 --> 00:05:17.689
And this fight is about
so much more than borders.

00:05:18.064 --> 00:05:20.650
Ukrainians are fighting for freedom,

00:05:20.692 --> 00:05:26.698
for our right to imagine and build
our future in our own way.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.326
Our people stand heroically.

00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:33.913
But against the second-largest
army in the world,

00:05:33.913 --> 00:05:36.708
we cannot stand alone.

00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:40.503
To end this war, we need you.

00:05:41.421 --> 00:05:47.135
We need every citizen in every nation
to demand that it stops.

00:05:49.512 --> 00:05:51.389
And that was my third lesson.

00:05:52.098 --> 00:05:56.185
My freedom is connected to yours.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:02.191
My daughter's first word
was the sound of destruction.

00:06:02.817 --> 00:06:04.652
But as she grows,

00:06:04.694 --> 00:06:07.780
I know she and the rest of her generation

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.199
will build Ukraine again.

00:06:11.242 --> 00:06:16.748
We will rehabilitate our roads,
our schools, our hospitals,

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:19.375
our houses and people.

00:06:20.335 --> 00:06:23.046
Fueled by knowledge and curiosity,

00:06:23.087 --> 00:06:28.217
we will walk again the path
to become a prosperous, free nation.

00:06:29.385 --> 00:06:32.847
If you stand with us.

00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:36.017
So please,

00:06:36.059 --> 00:06:37.936
don't watch from the side.

00:06:37.977 --> 00:06:39.687
Don't wait and see.

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:42.815
Stand up with us now.

00:06:42.857 --> 00:06:44.525
Stand up for freedom.

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:46.444
Stand up for democracy.

00:06:46.486 --> 00:06:49.197
Stand up for Ukraine.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.200
Thank you.

00:06:52.241 --> 00:06:59.248
(Applause)

